_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 14
---
order: 14
---
short_label: VII.14
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If there are any number of numbers, and others equal to them in multitude, which taken two and two together are in the same ratio, then they are also in the same ratio <i>ex aequali.</i>
----
proof:

Let there be as many numbers as we please *A, B,* and *C,* and others equal to them in multitude *D, E,* and *F,* which taken two and two are in the same ratio, so that *A* is to *B* as *D* is to *E,* and *B* is to *C* as *E* is to *F.*

I say that, *ex aequali A* is to *C* as *D* is to *F.*

<figure class="diagram">
